The `SessionCard` status badge is rendered in Line 1 of `packages/client/src/components/session/SessionCard.tsx` as a status chip containing the source icon and an overlaid `StatusShapeBadge`, with its color derived in `packages/client/src/lib/session/session-status-visuals.ts`.

### Exact Files

- **Rendering**: `packages/client/src/components/session/SessionCard.tsx`
- **Color and shape derivation**: `packages/client/src/lib/session/session-status-visuals.ts`
- **Theme color tokens**: `packages/client/src/lib/theme/themes.ts` and `packages/client/src/index.css`

---

### Where It Is Rendered

In `packages/client/src/components/session/SessionCard.tsx`:

- **Desktop view** (lines 846–854):
  ```tsx
  <span
    className={`relative inline-flex flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-[var(--bg-tertiary)] shadow-sm ${iconStatusColor}`}
    data-testid="session-status-icon"
    data-status-shape={statusShape}
    title={`${sourceLabels[session.source] ?? session.source} — ${session.status}`}
  >
    <Icon path={sourceIcons[session.source] ?? mdiConsoleLine} size={0.45} />
    <StatusShapeBadge shape={statusShape} colorClass={iconStatusColor} />
  </span>
  ```
- **Mobile view** (lines 683–691):
  ```tsx
  <span
    className={`relative flex-shrink-0 ${iconStatusColor}`}
    title={`${sourceLabels[session.source] ?? session.source} — ${session.status}`}
    data-testid="session-status-icon"
    data-status-shape={statusShape}
  >
    <Icon path={sourceIcons[session.source] ?? mdiConsoleLine} size={0.5} />
    <StatusShapeBadge shape={statusShape} colorClass={iconStatusColor} />
  </span>
  ```
- **`StatusShapeBadge`** definition (lines 119–131):
  Renders the shape glyph icon (`statusShapeIcon[shape]`) in an absolute corner badge using `colorClass` (`iconStatusColor`).

---

### How Its Color Is Chosen

The color is derived in two steps:

1. **`deriveDotColorWithFlags(session, flags)`** in `packages/client/src/lib/session/session-status-visuals.ts` (lines 100–111) computes the base background token by strict precedence:
   - `flags.hasError` → `"bg-[var(--status-error)]"`
   - `isChatRoutedAskUser(session, flags.hasWidgetBarPrompt)` (`currentTool === "ask_user"` when alive and not in a widget bar) → `"bg-[var(--status-needs-you)]"`
   - `session.resuming` → `"bg-[var(--status-working)] animate-pulse"`
   - `flags.isRetrying` → `"bg-[var(--status-working)] animate-pulse"`
   - `flags.hasNotice` → `"bg-[var(--status-notice)]"`
   - `statusColors[session.status]` map:
     - `streaming` → `"bg-[var(--status-working)] animate-pulse"`
     - `active` / `idle` → `"bg-[var(--status-idle)]"`
     - `ended` → `"bg-[var(--bg-surface)]"`
     - fallback → `"bg-[var(--bg-surface)]"`

2. **`deriveIconStatusColor(dotColor, status)`** in `packages/client/src/lib/session/session-status-visuals.ts` (lines 124–135) transforms the background class into text color:
   - If `status === "ended"` and `dotColor` starts with `"bg-[var(--bg-surface)]"`, it returns `"text-[var(--text-muted)]"`.
   - Otherwise, it replaces the leading `bg-` prefix with `text-` (e.g. `"text-[var(--status-working)] animate-pulse"`), which colors the icon and shape badge.

Theme CSS variables (`--status-needs-you`, `--status-working`, `--status-idle`, `--status-error`, `--status-notice`) resolve in `packages/client/src/lib/theme/themes.ts` to `--accent-purple`, `--accent-yellow`, `--accent-green`, `--accent-red`, and `--accent-blue`.
